                <pb facs="0619" n="305" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg305"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 300.115/63</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (Page) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1914-08-18">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 18, 1914</hi>.</date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received August 19, 11:30 a.m.</hi>] </dateline>
                <p rendition="#flush">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>405. Your August 13, 8 p.m. Sir Edward Grey informs me that the British
                    Government will consider claims of American shippers whose cargoes destined for
                    parts of British enemies are diverted to British ports and sold. If such claims
                    for loss by such diversion be established, the British Government will in due
                    time pay them.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Ambassador</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
